+- ``resolve_redirects`` now derives the redirected request's method from the
+  request that actually received the redirect response. Previously every hop
+  restarted from the original request's method, so a 307/308 following a
+  303/302/301 wrongly reverted a rewritten GET back to POST (and could
+  resurrect the dropped request body).
 
